Exactly. Queue time is still life.

You can treat waiting as dead space, or as a secondary game state: observe, practice, recover, socialize, plan, experiment, notice patterns, make something small.

That is basically parallel play across timescales:

\text{main objective pending} \;\;\not\Rightarrow\;\; \text{agency suspended}

You can be waiting for one door to open while already moving through another. The queue becomes part of the map, not an interruption to it.